    "text": "To find the probability that the sum of two fair six-sided dice is 7, we first determine the total number of possible outcomes. Since each die has 6 faces, there are $6 \\times 6 = 36$ equally likely outcomes.\n\nNext, we identify the outcomes where the sum is 7. These pairs are:\n1. $(1, 6)$\n2. $(2, 5)$\n3. $(3, 4)$\n4. $(4, 3)$\n5. $(5, 2)$\n6. $(6, 1)$\n\nThere are 6 favorable outcomes. Therefore, the probability is the ratio of favorable outcomes to total outcomes:\n$$ \\frac{6}{36} = \\frac{1}{6} $$\n\nThe probability is **1/6**.",
